& [Purpose]
  + implement SWA-06B2B1 as a safe synthetic-fixture-only source-reacquisition and current-registry persistence kernel over one exact SWA-06B2A receipt
  + prove bounded physical write mechanics without granting externally governed activation boot validation rollback live repository or provider authority

& [Upstream]
  + [SFP-001] completely validate cantor-succeeding-sop-activation-transaction-receipt/0.1 before physical contact
  + [SFP-002] require synthetic_fixture_only policy use transaction_correspondence_verified_awaiting_physical_execution status supplied_activation_plan_correspondence_only authority and every B2A physical result false
  + [SFP-003] retain the complete upstream request policy source registry transition supersession rollback obligations and digests without mutation

& [MarkerAndCommission]
  + [SFP-004] root marker profile is cantor-succeeding-sop-fixture-root-marker/0.1 with marker root recovery-owner evidence disposable live-repository live-activation and digest fields
  + [SFP-005] commission profile is cantor-succeeding-sop-fixture-persistence-commission/0.1 with commission root recovery-owner successor-snapshot receipt evidence fixture live-activation cleanup and digest fields
  + [SFP-006] require one through thirty-two unique evidence identities per form exact cross-form root and recovery-owner equality disposable true fixture_only true and every live_repository live_activation_allowed cleanup_authorized value false
  + [SFP-007] marker commission successor-snapshot and all distinct upstream duty identities remain distinct where roles differ

& [RootAndPaths]
  + [SFP-008] accept one explicit root Path argument only; production must not discover environment current directory clock process or network state
  + [SFP-009] canonical root is a real nonlink directory containing the exact marker and no root-level .git entry
  + [SFP-010] source final registry and temporary registry relative paths come exactly from the validated upstream receipt and pass its path grammar
  + [SFP-011] every existing traversed component is beneath the canonical root and is not a symbolic link or Windows reparse point; final and temporary parents are exact and the temporary leaf is absent

& [SourceAndRegistry]
  + [SFP-012] raw source bytes are reopened read without normalization bounded by local addressability and exactly match upstream byte count and SHA256 before registry mutation
  + [SFP-013] registry profile is cantor-succeeding-sop-fixture-registry-record/0.1 and embeds fixture root activation authority recovery owner optional last transaction exact current-registry snapshot and a domain digest
  + [SFP-014] predecessor registry record marker and root identities validate and its embedded snapshot equals the upstream current_registry exactly
  + [SFP-015] successor snapshot uses the commissioned distinct snapshot identity exact registry identity generation plus one proposal revision digest source path evidence and computed snapshot digest
  + [SFP-016] successor registry binds exact fixture root activation authority recovery owner transaction and successor snapshot and computes a separate registry-record digest

& [Persistence]
  + [SFP-017] deterministic successor machine bytes end in one LF and create_new the exact absent same-parent temporary path
  + [SFP-018] ordered execution is write_all sync_all reopen exact compare safe standard-library same-volume rename replacement parent directory sync_all and final reopen parse digest and exact compare
  + [SFP-019] before replacement a current-attempt owned temporary file is removed on failure; no other cleanup deletion or root removal is authorized
  + [SFP-020] after replacement any verification or durability failure reports replacement_performed true and does not claim rollback

& [ReceiptAndFault]
  + [SFP-021] success status is fixture_registry_persisted_awaiting_boot_validation and authority is synthetic_fixture_persistence_only with thirteen exact checks
  + [SFP-022] success binds upstream marker commission source predecessor successor and raw byte digests; physical_contact source_reacquired registry_observed registry_persisted current_sop_selected and temp_absent_after are true
  + [SFP-023] boot_activation_verified rollback_executed live_activation_performed provider_contacted model_called process_launched network_contacted and cleanup_performed are false
  + [SFP-024] typed atomic faults cover upstream marker commission identity root path link source registry temporary persistence durability post-write digest bound and machine-form failures while retaining physical_contact replacement_performed and owned_temp_removed state

& [DigestsFormsAndImplementation]
  + [SFP-025] marker commission registry and receipt use separate domain-separated lower-case canonical SHA256 identities
  + [SFP-026] machine forms deny unknown fields are bounded to 16777216 UTF-8 bytes and round-trip byte-identically after canonical production
  + [SFP-027] implementation is one safe cantor_ecosystem module one export one development-only synthetic upstream fixture example and producer plus focused semantic filesystem static and adversarial tests with no dependency or installed CLI delta
  + [SFP-028] production contains no unsafe environment clock process network provider model Git command remote boot parser rollback executor or caller-root cleanup surface

& [Acceptance]
  + [SFP-A01] source manifest input audit data design sixteen-threat review seven-fold exhaustion explosion justification matrix plan phase lock readiness review and this signature bind exactly
  + [SFP-A02] one recovery-owned disposable fixture proves exact source reacquisition predecessor observation same-parent durable replacement successor selection final reopen and deterministic receipt validation
  + [SFP-A03] adversarial fixtures refuse upstream status marker root recovery owner .git source tamper registry staleness existing temp link or reparse digest receipt authority unknown-field and oversize mutations
  + [SFP-A04] focused debug overflow-checked release warnings-denied Clippy format exact locked offline workspace recursive evidence attribution publication and post-push replay pass

& [DualHemisphere]
  + semantic hemisphere retains independent review policy source identity current and succeeding revisions supersession recovery ownership obligations and nonauthority
  + physical hemisphere performs only explicit disposable-fixture byte observation and registry replacement with exact partial-effect reporting
  + convergence is a synthetic fixture receipt awaiting boot validation and never a live current-SOP claim

& [Delineation]
  + exact B2A replay marker commission root boundary source bytes registry predecessor successor durable replacement final reopen receipt faults and evidence are inside
  + externally governed persistence hostile concurrent root locking boot validation rollback execution live activation provider model SWA-05 Git remote FPGA Minecraft cleanup and foreign work are outside

